desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Args Os"
	title_zh: "Args Os"
	type: vuln
	level: low
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-args-os"
	risk: "information-exposure"
	desc: <<<DESC
### 规则说明
args_os should not be used for security operations. From the docs: "The first element is traditionally the path of the executable, but it can be set to arbitrary text, and might not even exist. This means this property should not be relied upon for security purposes."

### 风险类型
敏感信息泄露（information-exposure）

### 影响
应用可能暴露内部路径、环境信息或敏感数据，攻击者可借此收集攻击面。

### 检测方式
Source 模式正则匹配，检测代码或配置中符合该风险模式的位置。

### 补充说明
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal pattern.

### 参考
- CWE: CWE-807: Reliance on Untrusted Inputs in a Security Decision
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
### 修复建议
限制敏感信息的输出范围，关闭不必要的调试接口，并对暴露内容进行脱敏。
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.rs": <<<POS
std::env::args_os()
POS
	"safefile://pos.rs": <<<NEG
std::env::args()
NEG
)

${*.rs}.pattern_regex(/(?:std::env::args_os\(\))/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "low",
	title: "Args Os",
	title_zh: "Args Os",
	message: "Args Os detected.",
}
